course: dictionary
lesson: 7017
title: Parliament: a group, a building, a flock of owls
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is meant. «They meet in a parliament, where they argue about ideas and vote on new laws.» Meet, argue, vote and laws are the clues. So a parliament here is a group of people who make the laws of a country.
explain: A capital letter can be a clue too. Parliament with a big P often means the building where the lawmakers meet, or the national parliament itself, as in «William Wilberforce argued in Parliament for years to end the slave trade.»
explain: Small p parliament can name a group of owls. Try your meaning in the sentence: «A parliament of owls sat on the branch.» Does it still make sense? A group of owls fits, and that is a good sign that you have the right meaning.
fact: A parliament is a group of people elected to make the laws of a country.
fact: Parliament, with a capital P, can also mean the building where they meet.
fact: In the United States, the law-making group is called Congress, not Parliament.
fact: «A parliament of owls» means a group of owls.
fact: Scotland and Wales let 16- and 17-year-olds vote in their own parliament and council elections.
exercise: «They meet in a parliament, where they argue about ideas and vote on new laws.» What is a parliament here? | A group of owls | A sort of bridge | *A group of people elected to make the laws of a country | A school break time
exercise: «A parliament of owls sat on the branch.» What does «a parliament of owls» mean? | A type of owl with a long tail | *A group of owls | A tree with many branches | A building full of birds
exercise: «William Wilberforce argued in Parliament for years to end the slave trade.» Where did he argue? | On a boat at sea | In a corner shop | At a football match | *In Parliament, where the elected lawmakers meet
test: «The Dáil is the main elected house of Ireland's Parliament.» What is the Dáil? | The prime minister of Ireland | A type of Irish food | *The main elected part of Ireland's Parliament
test: Which spelling is right for the UK's law-making body in «He works in London at ___»? | parlament | parliment | *Parliament | Parlaiment
exam: «In the United States it is called Congress, not Parliament.» What is the law-making body of the United States called? | Dáil | Taoiseach | *Congress | Houses of Parliament
